				"integrated_multimodal_description: [Shot 1] 3D CG, apocalyptic disaster film style, a wide aerial shot of a peaceful coastal city at sunrise. The camera tilts up with large amplitude at fast speed to reveal a massive meteor streaking across the sky, trailing a tail of fire and smoke, leaving a contrail that splits the clouds. The meteor grows rapidly larger as it descends. [Shot 2] At 00:03.500, the shot cuts to a ground-level wide shot as the meteor impacts the ocean just offshore. A colossal explosion of water and steam erupts, sending a mushroom-shaped cloud of vapor miles into the sky. The impact generates a massive shockwave that races across the water toward the city, followed by a towering tsunami wall. Buildings near the shore shatter from the shockwave before the water even arrives. [Shot 3] At 00:07.000, the shot cuts to a dramatic slow-motion close-up as the tsunami wave — hundreds of meters high — crashes over the city skyline, engulfing skyscrapers in churning white water and debris. Cars and entire buildings are swept away in the torrent.\n\noverall_soundscape: A piercing meteor entry whistle builds into a deafening ocean impact explosion with deep sub-bass rumble that shakes everything. The tsunami produces a continuous roaring wall-of-water sound with building-collapse crashes.\n\nnon_diegetic_music: A dramatic disaster score with slow-building low strings and brass that create dread, a massive percussion ensemble hit at impact, and then a solemn, sweeping orchestral melody that plays over the destruction with choir adding weight."
